Subject: image: each member's reach of the destinations kept, which its run host holds it to (D236, channel version 9)
Why: Hex's joint plan step 15 holds a harness to exactly the providers and the host its grants name. D236 keeps a destination image-wide, and each member reaches those of its own destinations that are kept, so a destination kept for one member is reached as well by every other member whose image names it; the orchestrator therefore names each member's reach (Narrowing::members) and the run host refuses before the VM starts a run in which any member the image declares would reach other than that (Hex's lead, 2026-11-12). Version 9, the next after Shards main's 7 (D241) and 8 (D242), written only where a reach is named, so a side of version 6 serves every other request.

